\title{Equivalence relations}
\date{2026-03-04T02:15:25Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{A very important class of [relations](008D) is \em{equivalence relations}, which in some suitable sense act like “a more general sort of equality”. We have used several of them this semester already!}

\transclude{008Z}

\p{I don’t know of a good way to explain why these particular properties are the “right” ones to capture “equality-like” things. But hopefully as we see some examples you will be convinced.}

\transclude{0094}
